    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0316" n="150" xml:id="pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1794</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the French Ambassador </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1969</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of August 4, 1917, relative to the proposals of the
                    Japanese Government concerning a consortium loan to China.</p>
                <p>In reply to your request for an expression of opinion as to the views of the
                    Government of the United States on the subject discussed in your note I have the
                    honor to state that the matter is having at present the careful consideration of
                    this Government which cannot at this time express an opinion relative
                    thereto.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
